### Rotating Card – CSS + HTML

Below is a minimal example that shows a card (a `div` with some content) that rotates 180 degrees around its Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to adjust the size, colors, or animation duration to fit your design.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card</title>
<style>
/* Container that keeps the card centered */
.wrapper {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center;
  align-items: center;
  height: 100vh;          /* full viewport height */
  background: #f0f0f0;
}

/* The card itself */
.card {
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  perspective: 800px;     /* gives depth to the 3D transform */

  /* Optional: add a subtle shadow */
  box-shadow: 0 10px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
}

/* Inner element that actually rotates */
.card-inner {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  background: #fff;
  border-radius: 12px;
  overflow: hidden;
  transition: transform 0.6s ease;   /* smooth rotation */
  transform-style: preserve-3d;      /* keep children in 3D space */
  position: relative;
}

/* Hover effect – rotate 180° around Y axis */
.card:hover .card-inner {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}

/* Front & back faces */
.card-face {
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden;   /* hide back face when rotated */
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center;
  align-items: center;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  font-size: 1.2rem;
  color: #333;
  padding: 20px;
  box-sizing: border-box;
}

.card-front {
  background: #fff;
}

.card-back {
  background: #fafafa;
  transform: rotateY(180deg);   /* start rotated so it becomes visible on hover */
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-inner">
      <!-- Front side -->
      <div class="card-face card-front">
        <h2>Front Side</h2>
        <p>Hover over this card to see the back.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Back side -->
      <div class="card-face card-back">
        <h2>Back Side</h2>
        <p>This is the other side of the card.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

#### How it works

1. **Perspective** – The `.card` container has `perspective: 800px;`. This gives the 3D effect when the inner element rotates.
2. **Transform style** – `.card-inner` uses `transform-style: preserve-3d;` so its children (`.card-face`) stay in 3D space.
3. **Backface visibility** – Each face has `backface-visibility: hidden;` so the hidden side disappears during rotation.
4. **Hover** – On hover, the inner element rotates 180 degrees around the Y‑axis, revealing the back face.

Feel free to replace the text, colors, or add more styling (e.g., gradients, images) to match your project’s look and feel.
